  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Find the parametric equations of the straight line that passes through $P(2,3,0)$ and is parallel to $v=\u27e83,\\,2,\\,0\u27e9.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ 2t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2+3t \\\\ 3+2t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2+3t \\\\ y=3+2t \\\\ z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
